        "original_id": "1705083c-85cb-59b2-a4b8-03545b8c64e4",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Luis Resto, Eminem, Don Was, Anita Baker, Patti Smith, Scott Silver, Curtis Hanson, Mekhi Phifer, Brittany Murphy, Michael Shannon, Kim Basinger\n- Roles: musician, producer, keyboardist, rapper, writer, director, actor\n- Works: The Eminem Show, 8 Mile\n- Topics: musical collaborations, film\n\nFacts:\n- Luis Edgardo Resto was born on July 22, 1961.\n- Luis Resto is an American musician, producer, and keyboardist.\n- Before 2001, Luis Resto played keyboards and co-wrote songs for artists including Anita Baker, Patti Smith, The Highwaymen, Vertical Horizon, and Fuel, including on many works produced by Don Was.\n- In 2001, Luis Resto began a prolific and lengthy collaboration with Eminem.\n- Since Eminem's third major-label album The Eminem Show, Luis Resto has worked closely with Eminem.\n- 8 Mile is a 2002 American drama film.\n- Scott Silver wrote 8 Mile.\n- Curtis Hanson directed 8 Mile.\n- Eminem, Mekhi Phifer, Brittany Murphy, Michael Shannon, and Kim Basinger starred in 8 Mile.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
